Equity Language Commons — License
==================================

The Equity Language Commons consists of three layers, each governed by a
different license. Pick the section that applies to what you're reusing.

------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Content layer (term pages, synthesis, chapter intros, the schema)

Copyright (c) 2026 Jordan Krueger

Licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
License (CC BY 4.0). You may share and adapt this material for any
purpose, including commercially, under the following terms:

  - Attribution — You must give appropriate credit ("Equity Language
    Commons, edited by Jordan Krueger"), provide a link to the license,
    and indicate if changes were made.

Full license text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode

This covers everything in:
  - site/src/content/terms/ (synthesis, audience notes, frontmatter
    composition)
  - site/src/content/sources/ (About sections, posture rationale)
  - site/src/content/chapters/ (lede, cross-cutting principles)
  - notes/ (schema documentation, working notes)
  - research/ (research notes — caveat: the AUDIT TRAIL of source
    quotes within research notes is fair-use citation, not commons-
    licensed content)

------------------------------------------------------------------------

